<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114382" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χονδρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>granular, coarse,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλευρα χονδρότερα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Mul.</u>
					2.193
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλφιτον ἀραιὸν καὶ χονδρόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					927b35
				</span></i>
			: mostly of <i>coarse</i> salt, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλες οὐ χονδροί, ἀλλὰ χαῦνοι καὶ
					λεπτοὶ ὥσπερ χιών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mete.</u>
					359a32
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χἄλα λήψεται χονδρόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phoen.
					2.5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χονδροὺς ἅλας</span> (cod.Rav.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χονδρὰς ἅλας</span>) is prob. in
				<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				521
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χόνδρους ἁλός</span>
			)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc"> χονδρός</span>
			Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χόνδρος</span>
			Subst. are distd. by Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.203
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.716
			</span></i>; 
				Comp.
			 and 
				Sup.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερος, -ότατος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
				<u>in Theod.</u>
				2.76H.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later, generally,
				<i>coarse,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρίχες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ps.-Callisth.
					2.33
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐηλάρια μικρὰ χοντρὰ</span>
			(sic) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Sammelb.</u>
					7033.39
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(v A. D.)</span>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χονδρός,</span>
			=
			<i>grossus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gloss.
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χόνδρος</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χονδρός</span> dissim. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χρονδ-ρο-,</span> cogn. with Engl.
				<i>grind.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
